<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shi Chaoyi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 763</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shi Chaoyi was the last ruler of the rebel Yan state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang dynasty</a>. He had his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shi-siming">Shi Siming</a> killed in 761 and took the throne, but lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> to Tang and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> forces in 762. Deserted by his generals, he killed himself in 763, ending the rebellion.</p></div>
